{"title":"Career Roadmap · Biomechanics Analyst","role":"Biomechanics Analyst","summary":"A Biomechanics Analyst applies engineering, physics, mathematics, human movement science, and data analysis to understand how the human body moves and performs.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Sports Engineering / Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Biomechanics Analyst applies engineering, physics, mathematics, human movement science, and data analysis to understand how the human body moves and performs."},{"type":"p","text":"In sports, the role involves analyzing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human movement and joint mechanics"},{"text":"Running, jumping, throwing, lifting and other athletic movements"},{"text":"Force, velocity, acceleration and power"},{"text":"Joint angles, range of motion and movement patterns"},{"text":"Ground reaction forces"},{"text":"Muscle and skeletal loading"},{"text":"Sports technique and performance"},{"text":"Injury-risk indicators"},{"text":"Wearable-sensor and motion-capture data"},{"text":"Equipment–athlete interaction"},{"text":"Rehabilitation and return-to-play movement"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["A strong graduate profile combines sports engineering","biomechanics","motion analysis","sensors","programming","statistics","machine learning."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A B.Tech/B.E. can prepare you for technical biomechanics, sports-performance and sports-technology roles. Clinical diagnosis, physiotherapy and medical rehabilitation responsibilities generally require the relevant professional qualification/licensing rather than an engineering degree alone."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech/B.E. Sports Engineering / Technology","Engineering + Human Anatomy + Physiology","Biomechanics + Kin