anics"}],[{"text":"Injury Biomechanics"},{"text":"Mechanical loading"},{"text":"Advanced biomechanics + research"}],[{"text":"Sports Technology R&D"},{"text":"Products + technology"},{"text":"Sensors + embedded + AI"}],[{"text":"Equipment Biomechanics"},{"text":"Athlete-equipment interaction"},{"text":"Mechanical testing + CAD"}],[{"text":"AI Sports Analytics"},{"text":"Movement + predictive analytics"},{"text":"ML + time-series analysis"}],[{"text":"High-Performance Sports"},{"text":"Elite athlete optimization"},{"text":"Sports science + analytics"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Final Career Equation"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Tech/B.E. Sports Engineering / Technology + Human Movement Science + Biomechanics + Kinematics/Kinetics + Motion Capture + Sensors + Signal Processing + Python/MATLAB + Statistics + Computer Vision + AI + Sports Performance Analysis + Practical Research/Internship = Job-Ready Biomechanics Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Best final profile"},{"type":"p","text":"A technically strong Sports Engineering graduate specializing in biomechanics, motion capture, force and wearable-sensor analysis, with Python/MATLAB, signal processing, computer vision, machine learning, sports-performance analytics and hands-on research or sports-technology experience."}]}]}